    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66825" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετανιπτρίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cup drunk after washing the hands</i> at the end of meals, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέξαι τηνδὶ μ. τῆς Υγιείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.Com.
					6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				149
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τῆς Υγιείας ἔγχεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nicostr.Com.
					3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. μεστὴν Διὸς Σωτῆρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diph.
					69
				</span></i>
			:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετανάστ-νιπτρον</span></b> , τό
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, δαίμονος ἀγαθοῦ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					137
				</span></i>
			.</div>
